hat contribute to weight loss. However, bariatric surgery also necessitates specific dietary adjustments post-operation and is associated with potential complications and nutritional issues. \n\nFurthermore, bariatric surgery is linked to various health outcomes, including impacts on cardiovascular disease and mortality rates among patients with obesity. It is often discussed in the context of Enhanced Recovery After Surgery (ERAS) protocols, which are designed to enhance recovery and minimize complications following the procedure. Overall, bariatric surgery encompasses a range of surgical interventions aimed at facilitating weight loss and improving overall health in individuals with obesity.\",72\r\n8442,NUTRITIONAL SUPPLEMENTS,\"Nutritional supplements are additional nutrients provided to patients when their dietary intake is insufficient for their health needs. They are particularly recommended for patients post-bariatric surgery to ensure adequate protein and nutrient intake. These products are also intended to enhance the diet of individuals with specific health conditions, such as cancer and diabetes, to improve nutritional intake and support recovery. Nutritional supplements are commonly used in clinical settings for patients with specific nutritional needs, offering a means to provide essential vitamins, minerals, and trace elements that may be lacking in their regular diet. Overall, nutritional supplements play a crucial role in enhancing dietary intake and ensuring that individuals receive the necessary nutrients for optimal health.\",6\r\n8430,LIQUID DIET,\"The \"\"LIQUID DIET\"\" refers to a specific dietary phase that is commonly implemented following bariatric surgery. This diet involves the consumption of only liquids, which is crucial for aiding recovery and adaptation after the surgical procedure. The primary purpose of the liquid diet is to protect the surgical sites and facilitate healing. It is characterized by small volumes of liquid intake, ensuring that patients can gradually reintroduce food while minimizing the risk of complications. Additionally, a liquid diet can also be prescribed for patients with certain medical conditions, emphasizing its role in various therapeutic contexts. Overall, the liquid diet serves as an essential step in the post-operative care of bariatric surgery patients, focusing on liquid or liquid-form foods to support their recovery process.\",3\r\n8536,SEMISOLID DIET,\"The \"\"SEMISOLID DIET\"\" is a dietary phase that follows the liquid diet, primarily designed for individuals transitioning back to solid foods. This phase consists of pureed or mashed foods, allowing for a gradual reintroduction of more solid textures. It is particularly relevant for patients who have undergone bariatric surgery, as it serves as a transitional stage where they can safely incorporate purées and soft foods into their diet. The semisolid diet plays a crucial role in helping individuals adjust their eating habits while ensuring proper nutrition during recovery.\",5\r\n8764,GASTRIC BYPASS,Gastric bypass is a surgical procedure for weight loss that alters the digestive system and can result in complications such as nutritional deficiencies.,3\r\n8768,BILIARY-PANCREATIC DIVERSION,,3\r\n5398,LANCET DIABETES ENDOCRINOL,\"Lancet Diabetes & Endocrinology is a specialized medical journal dedicated to research in the fields of diabetes and endocrine health. It publishes a wide range of studies, including those focused on non-alcoholic fatty liver disease, exploring its causes and treatment strategies. The journal also addresses topics related to differences in sex development and has published significant research on cardiovascular disease and mortality in patients with type 2 diabetes following bariatric surgery. Through its diverse array of articles, Lancet Diabetes & Endocrinology contributes to the advancement of knowledge and understanding in these critical areas of health.\",3\r\n8537,NORMAL CONSISTENCY DIET,\"The \"\"NORMAL CONSISTENCY DIET\"\" is the final phase following bariatric surgery, designed for patients to gradually reintroduce a variety of foods into their diet. During this phase, individuals are encouraged to focus on nutritional balance while consuming easily digestible solid foods. This diet allows for a broader range of food options, supporting the transition to a more typical eating pattern while still prioritizing the health and nutritional needs of the patient.\",2\r\n8759,ALCOHOL INTAKE,Alcohol intake is discouraged post-bariatric surgery due to its potential effects on nutrient absorption and the risk of addiction.,1\r\n8798,ALVAREZ,Alvarez J. is an author who provided nutritional recommendations for obesity in a manual published by Novartis Health Consumer S.A. in 2001.,1\r\n8787,BALTASAR,Baltasar A. is an author who discussed surgical treatment for morbid obesity in a publication in Cirugía Española in May 2004.,1\r\n8778,BAND GASTRIC,Band gastric is a type of bariatric surgery that involves placing a band around the stomach to restrict food intake.,1\r\n5963,CUMMINGS DE,Cummings DE is a researcher who has contributed to the understanding of metabolic surgery for the treatment of Type 2 diabetes in obese individuals.,1\r\n5964,RUBINO F,Rubino F is a researcher known for his work on metabolic surgery and its effects on Type 2 diabetes management.,1\r\n5976,TYPE 2 DIABETES REMISSION,\"Type 2 diabetes remission refers to the state where diabetes symptoms are no longer present, often discussed in the context of bariatric surgery outcomes.\",1\r\n6005,LAPAROSCOPIC SURGERY,\"Laparoscopic surgery is a minimally invasive surgical technique that uses small incisions and specialized instruments, often resulting in quicker recovery times.\",1\r\n6030,KWOCK CS,Kwok CS is an author of a study published in the International Journal of Cardiology regarding the long-term mortality in patients undergoing bariatric surgery.,1\r\n6031,GALLSTONES,\"Gallstones